{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1546567-initial-impression-of-gehenna-war-book","id":1546567,"title":"Initial impression of Gehenna War book.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-12-03T16:18:10-08:00","id":1546567,"title":"Initial impression of Gehenna War book.","content":"My first impression of the sourcebook is favorable as it brings the war of the ancients much closer to the New World and what are some of the signature characters thoughts on what is happening or what they think is starting with some of the cults.<br /> <br /> Some of the new merits and flaws make sense in this scenario and there is some additional character concept ideas to work with and I do like the additional powers and bonuses that my 11th generation Malkavian could learn though it does look like that high level elder and Methuselah powers are still off limits for the current setting.<br /> <br /> All in all it was a good purchase and see what stuff we can repurpose for our game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-03T20:17:39-08:00","id":1546570,"title":"","content":"I liked the book very much. I loved the ideas for elder Methuselah and Blood Gods powers, but I must say that I'm not a big fan of unstatted characters and powers. Also if they're going to keep Enkidu stateless, why did they bother make a character sheet for Mithras adapted to V5? Still it's by far my favourtrite V5 book, as it's at least a very good attempt to bring back the importance of the notion of &quot;cosmic horror&quot; to the setting (something V5 basically tryed to wipe out in the beginning).<br /> <br /> Me and my friends were even joking that for the idea for V5 to be &quot;street level&quot;, it's funny that their ideas for powers for Methusaleh and Blood Gods are sometimes even more impressivethan the ones we have in V20. Best v5 book so far, made me even think about adapting my table to V5 (but, it's unfortunately too much work for little gain, I still think).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-03T20:38:16-08:00","id":1546573,"title":"","content":"I didn't mind that Blood God's and really ancient Methuselah's being unstated as to leave a little mystery and your best chance of survival is hoping that they don't notice you at all.<br /> <br /> At least that is what my Malkavian would say about Blood God's like they listed in the sourcebook.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-03T20:42:31-08:00","id":1546574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1546567-initial-impression-of-gehenna-war-book?p=1546570#post1546570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I liked the book very much. I loved the ideas for elder Methuselah and Blood Gods powers, but I must say that I'm not a big fan of unstatted characters and powers. Also if they're going to keep Enkidu stateless,<b> why did they bother make a character sheet for Mithras adapted to V5?</b> Still it's by far my favourtrite V5 book, as it's at least a very good attempt to bring back the importance of the notion of &quot;cosmic horror&quot; to the setting (something V5 basically tryed to wipe out in the beginning).<br /> <br /> Me and my friends were even joking that for the idea for V5 to be &quot;street level&quot;, it's funny that their ideas for powers for Methusaleh and Blood Gods are sometimes even more impressivethan the ones we have in V20. Best v5 book so far, made me even think about adapting my table to V5 (but, it's unfortunately too much work for little gain, I still think).</div> </div> </div> </div>Self-indulgence, probably.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-03T21:59:50-08:00","id":1546577,"title":"","content":"I can go with that Saur Ops Specialist, I created my own 4th generation Malkavian that my character is descended from and as a excerise I did give him stats. Now I probably would leave that blank for future ancients.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-04T03:06:48-08:00","id":1546582,"title":"","content":"For what it's worth, when I ran TC I reverse engineered a formula for elder and methusleah experience allocation based on elder creation rules, published NPC Stat blocks, and storyteller rules of thumb for NPC generation. It held up exceedingly well until generating characters of 3,000 years of age or older, or so...at which point there started to be more experience points to spend than there were dots on the sheet, reasonable or otherwise.<br /> <br /> For funsies, i made Japheth according to his published (not canonically sensible) age by my formula. After giving him literally every attribute, ability, and discipline at 9 (accounting for out of clan cost), maxed virtues, every background available at 5, I still had about a thousand experience to spend. I had to conclude at that point, even bothering to stat out methuselahs is kind of pointless.<br /> <br /> Hilariously enough, ur-Shulgi is woefully weak as compared to what it should be according to White Wolf's own rules.<br /> <br /> &quot;Statless&quot; methuselahs isn't so much to preserve mystique, I think, as it is just shorthand for &quot;they have everything maxed, it's pointless to create a stat block to demonstrate this&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-04T12:29:39-08:00","id":1546600,"title":"","content":"Most Blood God's and Methuselah's would have their in clan Disciplines max out and one or two more near max with a smattering of elder level powers. At this point they're more of supernatural force of nature then anything human like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-04T13:12:14-08:00","id":1546601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1546567-initial-impression-of-gehenna-war-book#post1546567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My first impression of the sourcebook is favorable as it brings the war of the ancients much closer to the New World and what are some of the signature characters thoughts on what is happening or what they think is starting with some of the cults.<br /> <br /> Some of the new merits and flaws make sense in this scenario and there is some additional character concept ideas to work with and I do like the additional powers and bonuses that my 11th generation Malkavian could learn though it does look like that high level elder and Methuselah powers are still off limits for the current setting.<br /> <br /> All in all it was a good purchase and see what stuff we can repurpose for our game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the lore possibilities I\u2019ve heard about in Gehenna War, but I\u2019m turned off by the statement in the advertising that the book is mostly about how to run a high action chronicle. What do you think?<br /> <br /> Like how much of the book is about running a high-action combat chronicle versus the lore of the ancients and the powers of Methuselahs and Blood Gods?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":26996,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","user":"Amethyst","date":". 12-04-2024, 05:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-04T15:28:13-08:00","id":1546605,"title":"","content":"In my latest unapproved post, I asked Lysander for his advice on whether Gehenna War was a good buy. Just now, I went and reviewed the table of contents on Demiplane and I saw that only the first chapter was really interesting to me. Based on that, I decided once and for all not to buy it, especially since some of the lore on the ancients is available on the White Wolf wiki. Lysander, thanks anyway; I might ask you for your advice again sometime since I\u2019m impressed by your WoD knowledge. Have a great night.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-04T16:27:59-08:00","id":1546606,"title":"","content":"Thanks Amethyst, but I am far from a expert on WOD lore with some of the others on this forum. Though if use any of the Blood Cults at all we would change things around.<br /> <br /> FOr instance Ur-Shugi would be replaced by Izhim UR-Baal as he seems more fleshed out and dangerous then the Shepard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 12-04-2024, 07:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-04T17:00:22-08:00","id":1546609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1546567-initial-impression-of-gehenna-war-book?p=1546606#post1546606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks Amethyst, but I am far from a expert on WOD lore with some of the others on this forum. Though if use any of the Blood Cults at all we would change things around.<br /> <br /> FOr instance Ur-Shugi would be replaced by Izhim UR-Baal as he seems more fleshed out and dangerous then the Shepard.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest, if they're going to poorly stat such characters, then I rally prefer that they keep them unstatted. I sayd that because you just reminded me of the ridiculous stats Izhim Ur-Baal had in Children of the Night, funny enough the book was one of the first to give a set of rules to create NPC characters and yet they botched with one of the most important characters of the book, while bothering to make some ridiculous jokes like &quot;El Diablo Verde&quot; lol It's not an easy task to understand WW logic, but I swear I try.<br /> <br /> I honestly prefer to give stats to any important character in my story, be it a blood god or a neonate. If there's the possibility of interaction, then I like to have at least an idea of the characters capabilities. Of course many times I don't feel the need to give them a complete character sheet, it's always going to depend on how important the character is. <br /> <br /> I like giving my characters stats, it's an intereesting exercise and I also grew up as a child surrounded by rules lawyers, so I developed my ability to make good character sheets as a consequence. Of course nowadays as a confident ST (and adult) I don't feel any need to justify things, but old habits die hard. That has also helped me develop my ability to make good character's sheeets and even though nowadays I don't feel the need to &quot;combo&quot; things to make an &quot;OP character&quot; I still can do that better than most for laughs ofc, as this habit ended up making me get acquainted with basically every single power/merit ever published for Vampire/Mage/Werewolf/Changelings and in the end that made me read a lot of the lore of the setting since a young age.So there's that hahaha","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-04T17:04:16-08:00","id":1546611,"title":"","content":"Yes Izhim UR-Baal was given no max stats for any of skills, attributes and disciplines given his vast age. At the very least his in clan disciplines should be maxed out as much as a 5th generation kindred should be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-04T17:41:17-08:00","id":1546614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1546567-initial-impression-of-gehenna-war-book?p=1546611#post1546611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes Izhim UR-Baal was given no max stats for any of skills, attributes and disciplines given his vast age. At the very least his in clan disciplines should be maxed out as much as a 5th generation kindred should be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, It was honestly one of the worst I've seen in WW history, almost seemed like a joke that I didn't understand. I remember people often complained about Mithras stats, because they were released when the setting was very new and it was much weaker than it should (it's VERY HARD to imagine any prince of note without Auspex, let alone an &quot;\u00dcBERprince&quot; like Mithras). I could understand that it was because the setting was very young etc, but I cannot understand why they had to use the same character sheet for every occasion he reappered in the setting up until V20, like nobody dared to touch the &quot;sacred sriptures&quot; lol? Still, Mithras even with his pooly designed character sheet was god tier, but Izhim was on another level enrirely, his traits are simply bad, made no sense at all and had no such excuse as being &quot;a 1991 release&quot; lol, it was just a botch, one of the worst in this sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-04T18:14:56-08:00","id":1546616,"title":"","content":"Mithras didn't have a dot of Auspex to his portfolio of being a Blood God? Investment in Auspex is simply a smart way of improving your odds of success or survival of a high stress situation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-04T21:21:21-08:00","id":1546624,"title":"","content":"It's to bad that your post was flagged Amethyst and I couldn't attempt to answer any questions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-05T02:50:09-08:00","id":1546632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1546567-initial-impression-of-gehenna-war-book?p=1546600#post1546600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most Blood God's and Methuselah's would have their in clan Disciplines max out and one or two more near max with a smattering of elder level powers. At this point they're more of supernatural force of nature then anything human like.</div> </div> </div> </div>The situation is significantly worse than that. The rule of thumb has more or less always been to assign discipline dots equal to square root of age. That's well and good, until you get to the 3,000-year-old point.<br /> <br /> That's 55 discipline dots, rounding up. That gets you all three clan disciplines at level 9, some common discipline elder powers, and respectable levels of all common disciplines. That's fine.<br /> <br /> Then, you get to &quot;blood god&quot; Ur-Shulgi, Japheth, Baba Yaga, Yorak age. With Japheth (the youngest &quot;blood god&quot;) and his published age, that's 95 dots. At that point, you're running out of disciplines to justify giving these characters. The math just falls apart, and you're just better off assuming they have anything and everything they might need for a story's purposes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-05T04:03:06-08:00","id":1546634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1546567-initial-impression-of-gehenna-war-book?p=1546624#post1546624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's to bad that your post was flagged Amethyst and I couldn't attempt to answer any questions.</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s ok \ud83d\ude0a. Thank you anyway. I\u2019m satisfied with my decision to skip Gehenna War, but I\u2019m really looking forward to In Memoriam next year.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-05T10:40:41-08:00","id":1546652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1546567-initial-impression-of-gehenna-war-book?p=1546632#post1546632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The situation is significantly worse than that. The rule of thumb has more or less always been to assign discipline dots equal to square root of age. That's well and good, until you get to the 3,000-year-old point.<br /> <br /> That's 55 discipline dots, rounding up. That gets you all three clan disciplines at level 9, some common discipline elder powers, and respectable levels of all common disciplines. That's fine.<br /> <br /> Then, you get to &quot;blood god&quot; Ur-Shulgi, Japheth, Baba Yaga, Yorak age. With Japheth (the youngest &quot;blood god&quot;) and his published age, that's 95 dots. At that point, you're running out of disciplines to justify giving these characters. The math just falls apart, and you're just better off assuming they have anything and everything they might need for a story's purposes.</div> </div> </div> </div> I agree and that is disccounting Diablerie and if the vampire is an &quot;average joe&quot; or a genius. Because as in life, I like to think that there are simply vampires who are more capable than others, so according to the system even the &quot;average joe&quot; vampire would have perhaps too many points, now imagine the ones who develop faster than others, also diablerie in the equation, etc. I understand the point of &quot;not wasting time&quot; making such character's sheets, but then again I like to have it even if all I do is say &quot;X disciplines lv 9, every ability lv 9&quot; or like what the setting did with beings like Goratrix and Etrius &quot;(every path maxed as well as any ritual they might need for the purpose of the story), but then we still have &quot;something tangible&quot;, to not have a character sheet is still to me a problem, because it's like the character is &quot;just an idea&quot; and I like to remind myself of that, as we as writters sometimes run the risk of imagining that a story exists just because it's in our head, but no, it only &quot;exist&quot; if it's &quot;on paper&quot;, otherwise it's just an idea, not fully &quot;real&quot; (whatever that might mean lol).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-05T11:29:59-08:00","id":1546657,"title":"","content":"I agree with the notion that most Kindred were definitely not average people in life and had something that stood out that made them a good candidate for the embrace with a few outliers that didn't stand out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-05T12:00:15-08:00","id":1546660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1546567-initial-impression-of-gehenna-war-book?p=1546657#post1546657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree with the notion that most Kindred were definitely not average people in life and had something that stood out that made them a good candidate for the embrace with a few outliers that didn't stand out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good that we agree. One of the main reasons I like to give stats to my characters is the one I wrote in my post, when I don't write anything about the caracter's traits, it feels like the character is &quot;just an idea&quot;, like a story in my head, I need to write something there, even if it's just as I said, &quot;every path of thaumaturgy maxed out and every ritual they might need for the purpose of the story&quot;, etc. To not write anything there doesn't feel good for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-05T13:54:49-08:00","id":1546664,"title":"","content":"True they all began as an idea and putting it to paper or a word processor helps make them feel more fleshed out. My one character in another game setting I had put together notes of where he spent his childhood, how many siblings, why he chooses his way of life and what kind of relationship he has between his family and superiors.<br /> <br /> I know that sometimes focusing to much on relationship and not on adventure can be trouble, but I try to keep the initial idea simple and add to it over time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-05T16:40:45-08:00","id":1546667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1546567-initial-impression-of-gehenna-war-book?p=1546664#post1546664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True they all began as an idea and putting it to paper or a word processor helps make them feel more fleshed out. My one character in another game setting I had put together notes of where he spent his childhood, how many siblings, why he chooses his way of life and what kind of relationship he has between his family and superiors.<br /> <br /> I know that sometimes focusing to much on relationship and not on adventure can be trouble, but I try to keep the initial idea simple and add to it over time.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's my approach as well, then I make files about them and their interctions with other NPCs and depending on their importance I even write short stories about them, with my most important characters I do it, to the point where I even joke with my players that &quot;I'm making scenes with my NPCs, so always beware that if the group doesn't do anything, the NPCs are going to do something about it&quot;. I make it because one of the things I always like to emphasize in my stories is that the &quot;worlds keeps turning&quot;, so there's always something happening behind the scenes. <br /> <br /> Regarding your commentary about relationships, I fel like WoD games, imo especially vampire, is a lot character's driven, so it's rarely a waste of time to invest in characters. I used to tell ST that were beginning to ST the game and asking advice (since I'm playing for such a long time and I actively take part in many events) that if you want to &quot;shake things up&quot; with a given story, add an interesting and deep character to the plot, it almost always works like a charm, players get invested and it changes the dynamics of the game and sometimes a single &quot;not so thrilling&quot; game session can become very much alive with a good introduction to an intereting character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-06T11:33:12-08:00","id":1546697,"title":"","content":"I picked up the Sabbat book and Second Inquisition today. They both look pretty good. I didn\u2019t buy the Players Guide because my friend said I probably wouldn\u2019t like it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-06T12:07:40-08:00","id":1546699,"title":"","content":"Myself I enjoyed the Players Guide and some of the updated rules for Blood Potency and having the other clans like Banu Haqim, Hecate, Ministry, Lasombra, and the other non Camarilla clans. Also having additional options for alternative clan banes and explaining how Visscuitde works under the Protean umbrella.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-06T12:27:06-08:00","id":1546701,"title":"","content":"But aren\u2019t the rules for the other clans found in other places (Lasombra in Chicago by Night, Banu Haqim in Camarilla book, Ministry in Anarchs book, Hecata in Cults of the Blood Gods, Tzimisce in Sabbat book, Ravnos I forget where but I know I\u2019ve seen them somewhere) and grouped together in the Players Guide for ease of reference? That\u2019s a big reason my friend thought I wouldn\u2019t like it. I already own most of those, so that info would be duplicative for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-06T12:32:08-08:00","id":1546702,"title":"","content":"They are Amethyst, but for ease of reference is why I like the Players Guide and it expands more on the clan attitude and having additional Discipline powers and Amalgams is a plus for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-07T11:08:12-08:00","id":1546735,"title":"","content":"Players is a useful compilation, sabbat is...less so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":